Project live_indo_react_reactions {
    database_type: 'PostgreSQL'
    Note: '''
Anonymous, topic-scoped reactions. One row represents one accepted submission
with exactly one polling answer, a resolved Indonesian province, optional comment
text, and at most one provider-hosted GIF reference. This DBML is the schema design;
paired SQL files in reaction_database/migrations implement it. The reaction_database
executable applies tracked migrations and verifies prerequisites, inserting no
production reactions. There is no seed catalog or seed_history table here. The
reaction submission service is not implemented by this preparation tool.

External references:
topic_id identifies master_database.topics.id. Region codes identify master
provinces/cities by Kemendagri code, not generated IDs. These are separate databases:
there are deliberately no SQL foreign keys or local reference-table copies here.
reaction_service validates topic availability, polling-method agreement, selection
index bounds, region existence, and city/province membership before insertion.
The service also validates which answer column belongs to each polling method.
Store the polling-method code as indexed text, without an enum or a hard-coded
method-to-column CHECK. New method codes do not require an enum migration; the
service owns their interpretation. Exactly one of the current answer columns is
required. A new answer shape may require a separate schema change.
selection stores a zero-based integer option index, not its label. The service
checks it against the topic's selection_options array length and maps index 0 to
PostgreSQL array position 1. Master-service policy freezes topic methods and option
ordering/content after responses exist and preserves polling-method code meanings.

Location and admission policy:
reaction_service rejects requests whose IP country is outside Indonesia or cannot
be resolved, even when supplied coordinates are inside Indonesia. An accepted
request must also resolve an Indonesian province; city/regency resolution is
optional. Resolve regions from supplied coordinates when used, otherwise from IP
geolocation, and record the source. These country/admission checks are service
responsibilities; no database business triggers are planned.
coordinates stores only a user-supplied 2D WGS84 point, never an IP estimate.
location_source describes how the region codes were resolved; supplied coordinates
may still be present when IP resolution was used. Enable PostGIS before creating
this table: CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS postgis;
Use geometry(Point,4326), with longitude X and latitude Y. Construct points with
ST_SetSRID(ST_MakePoint(longitude, latitude), 4326) only for already-WGS84 input;
ST_SetSRID does not reproject coordinates. Transform other source CRSs explicitly.
Use the GiST index for bounding-box/intersection queries against coordinates.
Geometry distances in SRID 4326 are in degrees, not metres. Metre-based distance
queries require geography or a suitable projected CRS; casting to geography does
not automatically use this geometry GiST index.
request_ip is an IPv4/IPv6 host address determined by the service using its trusted
proxy configuration, not blindly copied from caller-controlled forwarded headers.
Raw IP and precise coordinates are internal metadata: exclude them from public
feeds, API response DTOs, broadcasts, and routine logs.

Write and read behavior:
The service owns id/submitted_at and treats accepted payloads, original location,
and submission time as immutable. deleted_at supports later soft deletion for
moderation. There is no is_active or updated_at field. GIF-reference validation, optional-text
normalization, and payload limits belong to reaction_service; no arbitrary text
length limit is defined here. This schema does not identify users or restrict
reactions by IP. No accounts, aggregates, outbox, or database-to-network delivery
guarantee is implied.

GIF references:
Store gif_provider and gif_id together or neither; do not persist a rendition/CDN
URL as the durable reference. Both values must be nonblank when present. Provider
codes are flexible text, for example klipy or giphy; reaction_service validates the
supported provider and content identifier. No provider is selected by this ERD.
Broadcast the reference with the reaction. The frontend resolves current media
through the provider-approved integration and loads the supplied media URL without
rewriting its parameters. Do not assume permission to cache URLs/assets, proxy,
or rehost media. Handle removed/unavailable GIFs without discarding the reaction.
No separate GIF table or GIF-reference index is needed for this initial design.

Start with one physical table because traffic and retention estimates are unknown.
Use server-generated BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY for id in migrations;
DBML increment exports GENERATED BY DEFAULT (or BIGSERIAL in older exporters);
adjust it to GENERATED ALWAYS explicitly.
This design alone is not a measured throughput guarantee. Introduce partitioning
only after measuring workload/growth and choosing retention. Future time partitioning
requires revisiting the primary key: PostgreSQL requires the partition key in a
partitioned table's primary/unique constraints; id alone would not suffice.

The two feed indexes below describe keys; DBML cannot express their partial
predicates. Replace exported full-index definitions with these exact SQL forms:
CREATE INDEX idx_reactions_topic_feed ON reactions (topic_id, submitted_at, id) WHERE deleted_at IS NULL;
CREATE INDEX idx_reactions_topic_province_feed ON reactions (topic_id, province_kemendagri_code, submitted_at, id) WHERE deleted_at IS NULL;
Do not create both full and partial versions. For descending keyset pagination use
WHERE topic_id = $1 AND deleted_at IS NULL
AND (submitted_at, id) < ($cursor_time, $cursor_id)
ORDER BY submitted_at DESC, id DESC LIMIT $limit;
Omit the cursor predicate for the first page. Province feeds also filter the
province code. B-tree backward scans supply the descending order after equality
filters on leading columns. Timestamp plus ID gives a deterministic tie-breaker.
Also create the spatial index below; DBML does not express the GiST index type:
CREATE INDEX idx_reactions_coordinates_gist ON reactions USING GIST (coordinates);
The GIS type must be unquoted geometry(Point,4326), not a quoted identifier
containing its parameters, if the DBML exporter quotes the custom type.
Do not substitute a B-tree index on coordinates. This GiST index supports spatial
queries across stored points; apply deleted_at filters when querying visible rows.
The polling_method_code index is an ordinary full B-tree index. No standalone IP,
city, text-search, or deleted_at indexes are proposed without a query requiring
them. Partial feed indexes cover visible rows.

References:
https://postgis.net/docs/using_postgis_dbmanagement.html
https://postgis.net/docs/using_postgis_query.html
https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/datatype-net-types.html
https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/indexes-multicolumn.html
https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/indexes-partial.html
https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/ddl-partitioning.html
'''
}

Enum reaction_location_source {
    coordinates [note: 'Province/city resolved from user-supplied coordinates.']
    ip [note: 'Province/city estimated from the request IP.']
}

Table reactions [headercolor: #F97316] {
    Note: 'One accepted anonymous polling answer with optional text/GIF. External topic/region references are validated by reaction_service. Payloads are immutable by service policy; deleted_at controls feed visibility.'

    id                       bigint [pk, increment, note: 'Server-generated identity; SQL migrations use GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY.']
    topic_id                 bigint [not null, note: 'External master_database.topics.id; no cross-database foreign key.']
    polling_method_code      text [not null, note: 'Flexible method-code snapshot; reaction_service validates method and answer compatibility.']
    agree_disagree           boolean [note: 'Nullable; false is a populated answer.']
    rating                   smallint [note: 'Nullable integer from 0 through 10.']
    selection                integer [note: 'Nullable zero-based topic option index; reaction_service validates array bounds.']
    comment                  text [note: 'Optional comment; normalize absent/blank input in the service.']
    gif_provider             text [note: 'Optional provider code, e.g. klipy or giphy. Required together with gif_id.']
    gif_id                   text [note: 'Optional opaque provider content ID, not a media URL. Required together with gif_provider.']
    coordinates              geometry(Point,4326) [note: 'Optional nonempty 2D WGS84 user point; X longitude, Y latitude. GiST index SQL in project note. Internal only.']
    request_ip               inet [not null, note: 'Service-resolved IPv4/IPv6 client host address. Internal only.']
    province_kemendagri_code varchar(2) [not null, note: 'Required resolved Indonesian province code. External master reference.']
    city_kemendagri_code     varchar(5) [note: 'Optional resolved city/regency PP.CC code. External master reference.']
    location_source          reaction_location_source [not null]
    submitted_at             timestamptz [not null, default: `NOW()`, note: 'Server-assigned submission timestamp; never caller controlled.']
    deleted_at               timestamptz [note: 'Null means visible; soft deletion does not change the original submission.']

    Indexes {
        polling_method_code [name: 'idx_reactions_polling_method_code']
        (topic_id, submitted_at, id) [name: 'idx_reactions_topic_feed', note: 'Partial B-tree WHERE deleted_at IS NULL; exact SQL in project note.']
        (topic_id, province_kemendagri_code, submitted_at, id) [name: 'idx_reactions_topic_province_feed', note: 'Partial B-tree WHERE deleted_at IS NULL; exact SQL in project note.']
    }

    Checks {
        `(gif_provider IS NULL) = (gif_id IS NULL)` [name: 'ck_reactions_gif_reference_pair']
        `gif_provider IS NULL OR gif_provider !~ '^[[:space:]]*$'` [name: 'ck_reactions_gif_provider_not_blank']
        `gif_id IS NULL OR gif_id !~ '^[[:space:]]*$'` [name: 'ck_reactions_gif_id_not_blank']
        `topic_id > 0` [name: 'ck_reactions_topic_id_positive']
        `num_nonnulls(agree_disagree, rating, selection) = 1` [name: 'ck_reactions_exactly_one_answer']
        `rating IS NULL OR rating BETWEEN 0 AND 10` [name: 'ck_reactions_rating_range']
        `selection IS NULL OR selection >= 0` [name: 'ck_reactions_selection_index_nonnegative']
        `length(btrim(polling_method_code)) > 0` [name: 'ck_reactions_polling_method_not_blank']
        `coordinates IS NULL OR (NOT ST_IsEmpty(coordinates) AND ST_IsValid(coordinates) AND ST_X(coordinates) BETWEEN -180 AND 180 AND ST_Y(coordinates) BETWEEN -90 AND 90)` [name: 'ck_reactions_coordinates_valid']
        `location_source <> 'coordinates' OR coordinates IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_reactions_coordinate_source']
        `province_kemendagri_code ~ '^[0-9]{2}$'` [name: 'ck_reactions_province_code_format']
        `city_kemendagri_code IS NULL OR city_kemendagri_code ~ '^[0-9]{2}[.][0-9]{2}$'` [name: 'ck_reactions_city_code_format']
        `city_kemendagri_code IS NULL OR substring(city_kemendagri_code FROM 1 FOR 2) = province_kemendagri_code` [name: 'ck_reactions_city_province_prefix']
    }
}
